  },
  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating to put in the effort to stain your beautiful log home interior, only to find it looks uneven or blotchy. This often happens because of a few common mistakes that are actually pretty easy to avoid. One big culprit is not properly prepping the wood beforehand. If you have existing coatings that are incompatible with your new stain, or if you've spot-sanded only certain areas, the new stain won't adhere evenly, leading to those unsightly blotches. Also, trying to apply a new stain color right over an old one without proper removal or prep is a recipe for disaster. Different stains react differently, and without a clean slate, you'll struggle to get a uniform look. You want to make sure the wood is dry and clean across the entire area you're working on. Think of it like painting a wall – you wouldn't just clean one small section, right? For the best results, it's about a consistent approach to surface preparation. When you're dealing with a large log home or significant prep needs, sometimes calling in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can really make a difference, ensuring everything is prepped correctly for a beautiful, even finish.",
